            <ArticleTitle>[Anatomy, physiology and clinical examination of the shoulder].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1383-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Shoulder pain is usually caused by periarthritis. Impingement syndrome and frozen shoulder (adhesive capsulitis) are the more frequently clinical aspect observed. A shoulder standardised clinical examination often give a precise lesional diagnostic. Complementary examinations are useful to distinguish other cause of shoulder pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
